From 4b738f4f51bc47778cd8dfd7125ae0802399cd7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:42:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: apple: Hold ANS reset during controller removal

The controller removal path asserted and immediately deasserted ANS reset.
On T8132 this left the subsequent Linux boot stuck before SART probe
completed, after U-Boot had successfully read the kernel and initramfs.

Hold reset for 10 microseconds, matching m1n1's ANS reset sequence. A
matched build without the delay reproduces the stall; the delayed reset
boots Linux through U-Boot's EFI stub path and mounts its NVMe root.

Validated on an M4 Mac mini with the 25G83 firmware and the development
7.1.13-ARCH #109 kernel, with and without the DockChannel early console.

The reset hold follows Hector Martin's m1n1 commit a5a57c230e7f
("pmgr: Add pmgr_adt_reset()"). The tested duration matches m1n1;
it is not a measured minimum reset pulse width.

Link: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/m1n1/commit/a5a57c230e7fb4884c30045ee0fb9372329469a9
Assisted-By: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra)
Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
---
 drivers/nvme/nvme_apple.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/nvme_apple.c b/drivers/nvme/nvme_apple.c
index a83c32674cf..35f76af2952 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/nvme_apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/nvme_apple.c
@@ -311,6 +311,8 @@ static int apple_nvme_remove(struct udevice *dev)
 	priv->sart = NULL;
 
 	reset_assert_bulk(&priv->resets);
+	/* Give the ANS reset time to reach the device before releasing it. */
+	udelay(10);
 	reset_deassert_bulk(&priv->resets);
 
 	return 0;
-- 
